+No P0.
+
+### P1
+
+- **Debate is wrongly excluded.** Its identity search and claim search are separate calls: pass A receives only title/byline metadata, while pass B independently receives the full article and asks the model to “pick a few claims” ([src/debate.ts:1894](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbk930hy-paperwork-all-modes/src/debate.ts:1894), [src/debate.ts:1916](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbk930hy-paperwork-all-modes/src/debate.ts:1916), [src/debate.ts:1279](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbk930hy-paperwork-all-modes/src/debate.ts:1279)). Apply `pick` only to `CLAIMS_SYSTEM`; it cannot interfere with identity search. “Low risk” and a pinned stamp are not principled exemptions. This would require `debate/5→6` and updating its literal assertion ([tests/debate.test.ts:1302](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbk930hy-paperwork-all-modes/tests/debate.test.ts:1302)). The other exclusions are defensible: citations, referee work, asked modes, cross-references/title claims, and labels each legitimately consume paperwork.
+
+- **Illustrated can still repaint an old, paperwork-bearing Sketch.** Its prompt requires one plate for every supplied scene ([src/illustrated.ts:819](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbk930hy-paperwork-all-modes/src/illustrated.ts:819)), but an older Sketch is merely `outdated`, not source-stale. Illustrated’s readiness check ignores `outdated` ([src/web/useIllustrated.ts:456](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbk930hy-paperwork-all-modes/src/web/useIllustrated.ts:456)), and the server refuses only a source-stale Sketch ([src/pipeline.ts:4311](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbk930hy-paperwork-all-modes/src/pipeline.ts:4311)). Thus “Paint again” can combine “leave paperwork out” with “paint every old scene.” Require a current Sketch, offer redraw-then-paint when it is outdated, or explicitly define how an inherited paperwork scene is handled. The eval must test this migration path, not only Illustrated paired with a freshly generated same-arm Sketch.
+
+- **The Arc stamp has an unacknowledged automatic cost.** Contrary to “Arc is regenerated only when the pipeline runs,” opening any owned article with an older Arc automatically queues an unforced Arc job ([src/web/useArc.ts:163](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbk930hy-paperwork-all-modes/src/web/useArc.ts:163)). Its own freshness check also rejects a version mismatch ([src/arc.ts:283](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbk930hy-paperwork-all-modes/src/arc.ts:283)). So `arc/6→7` spends money automatically, once per affected article when its owner next opens it. The bump is semantically right, but the plan must acknowledge and accept that rollout.
+
+- **The block-id screen is not sound as one generic “item” test.** It is sound for FAQ, Quiz, Ideas and Timeline, whose items require anchored passages/occurrences, and for stored Quotes, whose `blockId` is derived by code ([src/types.ts:4765](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbk930hy-paperwork-all-modes/src/types.ts:4765), [src/types.ts:4583](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbk930hy-paperwork-all-modes/src/types.ts:4583), [src/types.ts:859](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbk930hy-paperwork-all-modes/src/types.ts:859), [src/types.ts:3941](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbk930hy-paperwork-all-modes/src/types.ts:3941), [src/types.ts:1038](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbk930hy-paperwork-all-modes/src/types.ts:1038)). But:
+
+  - Sketch nodes have optional blocks, while captions, labels, regions and edges have none ([src/sketch-scene.ts:124](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbk930hy-paperwork-all-modes/src/sketch-scene.ts:124)).
+  - Illustrated vignettes are anchored, but plate titles and the image composition prompt are not ([src/illustrated-plate.ts:298](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbk930hy-paperwork-all-modes/src/illustrated-plate.ts:298), [src/illustrated-plate.ts:367](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbk930hy-paperwork-all-modes/src/illustrated-plate.ts:367)).
+  - Glossary entries do have computed `blocks`; saying they cite none throws away the strongest available screen ([src/types.ts:598](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbk930hy-paperwork-all-modes/src/types.ts:598), [src/glossary.ts:693](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbk930hy-paperwork-all-modes/src/glossary.ts:693)).
+  - Arc entries have a block range, so a paperwork-only part can be classified deterministically rather than by regex ([src/types.ts:313](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbk930hy-paperwork-all-modes/src/types.ts:313)).
+
+  Define a per-mode extractor and separately read unanchored prose. Mark only blocks that are wholly paperwork; the shared rule expressly makes mixed funding/method/limit passages content ([src/paperwork.ts:89](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbk930hy-paperwork-all-modes/src/paperwork.ts:89)).
+
+### P2
+
+- **`pick` is broadly correct, but “Take nothing from it” is unnecessarily absolute.** The by-role clause and the explicit “someone the content also names” sentence protect the examples in the question: a body-discussed person remains a glossary candidate; a body-narrated event remains a timeline event; funding used as method/evidence/limit is content. Still, the wording could prevent using a bibliography’s full name or alias to disambiguate a person independently selected from the body. Safer: “Choose no item solely from paperwork; anchor every selected item in content,” while retaining the present FAQ/Quiz/evidence prohibition.
+
+- **`part` is the right Arc kind and its schema can carry it, but reconcile the exceptions explicitly.** Arc requires one string per physical part and pairs it by index, so a label such as “The references.” fits ([src/arc.ts:105](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbk930hy-paperwork-all-modes/src/arc.ts:105), [src/arc.ts:206](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbk930hy-paperwork-all-modes/src/arc.ts:206), [src/arc.ts:309](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbk930hy-paperwork-all-modes/src/arc.ts:309)). But it otherwise requires every sentence to be relational, bans part titles, and gives the physical first/last parts special jobs ([src/arc.ts:129](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbk930hy-paperwork-all-modes/src/arc.ts:129), [src/arc.ts:133](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbk930hy-paperwork-all-modes/src/arc.ts:133), [src/arc.ts:146](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbk930hy-paperwork-all-modes/src/arc.ts:146)). State that the label is an exception to all three and test leading and trailing paperwork parts.
+
+- **The coverage test is a useful default, not a complete detector.** Bare-identifier AST matching ([tests/plain-words-coverage.test.ts:52](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbk930hy-paperwork-all-modes/tests/plain-words-coverage.test.ts:52)) misses renamed imports, member calls, wrappers, pre-rendered article strings, and custom renderers such as Structure/Labels. It also catches non-prompt uses such as `crossrefs-fingerprint`. Keep it, but add a known prompt-files-without-a-call list like the plain-words test and document false positives as well as false negatives.
+
+- **All nine proposed bumps are semantically justified, including Quiz.** This changes what may be a question, exactly the threshold its comment sets ([src/quiz.ts:585](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbk930hy-paperwork-all-modes/src/quiz.ts:585)). Implementation must bump Sketch in `sketch-scene.ts`, Illustrated in `illustrated-plate.ts`, and Arc in `arc-version.ts`, because those import-free constants are also client-facing ([src/sketch-scene.ts:57](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbk930hy-paperwork-all-modes/src/sketch-scene.ts:57), [src/illustrated-plate.ts:132](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbk930hy-paperwork-all-modes/src/illustrated-plate.ts:132), [src/arc-version.ts:1](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbk930hy-paperwork-all-modes/src/arc-version.ts:1)). Update Quiz’s literal test ([tests/quiz.test.ts:140](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbk930hy-paperwork-all-modes/tests/quiz.test.ts:140)). Also note that Illustrated’s version is part of its input fingerprint, so the bump reports existing plates stale as well as outdated ([src/illustrated.ts:246](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbk930hy-paperwork-all-modes/src/illustrated.ts:246)); regenerating Quotes can break saved quote links unless exactly the same words are selected again ([src/quotes.ts:1642](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbk930hy-paperwork-all-modes/src/quotes.ts:1642)).
+
+- **Arm design is adequate but the judging gate is too narrow.** One `after` draw is consistent with the guide; add `after-2` only on a close result. However, judging only mode/article cells with baseline paperwork cannot detect collateral loss in clean cells. Blind-read at least one representative pair per mode plus every baseline leak and the scaling boundary. For Illustrated, inject its supported stub painter so only the production brief call is paid for ([src/illustrated.ts:1102](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbk930hy-paperwork-all-modes/src/illustrated.ts:1102)); that is cheaper and equally probative for this prompt change.
+
+**Verdict: revise before build—chiefly add Debate, fix the Illustrated dependency, acknowledge Arc’s automatic spend, and make the measurement mode-specific.**
